       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, or shock.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **10 mg once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose. Some patients start at 2.5 mg, such as frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf 50 mg was a typo, tell me the dose you meant and I'll enter it. If you want a dose above the labeled maximum, that needs to go through your pharmacy and the prescriber's usual process. I can't enter it based on an unverified claim of approval."
