       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. Amlodipine's FDA-approved label gives a maximum dose of 10 mg once daily for adults. I can't verify what you've said about the label, and it doesn't match the label I know. 50 mg is five times that maximum.\n\nOverdose at this level can cause profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock. It can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and amlodipine's long half-life makes those effects last.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the labeled maximum.\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated up.\n\nIf you think the label has changed, please check the current prescribing information with your pharmacy. If a dose above the labeled maximum is clinically needed, the prescriber and pharmacy will need to review it and handle it outside this tool. Tell me which of the doses above you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
